WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.140
Police gunned down the alleged killer Cherif
Chekatt....in Strasbourg's Neudorf neighourhood.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:10.040
The 29-year-old grew up here.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:15.099
Security forces finally caught up with him
on Thursday evening, a full two days after

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:21.470
the attack on the city's popular Christmas
market.

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:26.160
This individual matched the description of
the person wanted since Tuesday evening.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.770
They arrested him.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:31.990
The moment they tried to arrest him, he turned
around and opened fire.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:42.620
They then responded and managed to shoot him
downCherif Chekatt was already known to police

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:49.030
for his long criminal record and radical Islamist
beliefs, before he indiscriminately open fire

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:54.229
near the Christmas market.

00:00:54.229 --> 00:00:58.589
But he managed to escape.

00:00:58.589 --> 00:01:02.149
Security has been heavy in Strasbourg since
then.

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:07.460
Now people say they're relieved it's finally
safe to go out.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:14.040
Everybody is quite happy to know that the
killer has been finally shot.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:21.460
And I think now the city and life can keep
going on in Strasbourg.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:24.570
The Christmas market is reopening on Friday.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:29.200
France remains on high alert in the wake of
the large number of terrorist attacks, which

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:35.670
have shocked the country in recent years.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:40.640
Tuesday's attack has left Strasbourg in mourning,
but determined not to give in despite the

00:01:40.640 --> 00:06:03.560
latest terrorist outrage.

